<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bangkusay Channel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3 June 1571</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Bangkusay</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bangkusay Channel was fought on 3 June 1571 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> Bay, off Tondo near the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pasig-river">Pasig River</a>. A fleet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagalog-language">Tagalog</a> and Kapampangan warriors led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarik-sulayman">Tarik Sulayman</a> of Macabebe attacked the Spanish under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-de-goiti">Martín de Goiti</a> and was defeated, Sulayman being killed. The victory secured Spanish control of Manila, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-lopez-de-legazpi">Miguel López de Legazpi</a> formally founded as a Spanish city later that month.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bangkusay-channel.jpg" alt="Battle of Bangkusay Channel" width="320" height="469" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kej Andrés (Ryomaandres) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Memorare_(Battle_of_Bangkusay),_Tondo_NHCP_Historical_Marker.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
